1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:08,025
On the night of March thirteenth, nineteen ninety-seven, thousands of people in Arizona looked up and saw lights.

2
00:00:08,025 --> 00:00:10,816
Five of them, in a V, gliding in silence.

3
00:00:10,816 --> 00:00:13,266
Some swear it blocked out the stars.

4
00:00:13,733 --> 00:00:16,128
A craft a mile wide, they said.

5
00:00:16,128 --> 00:00:21,844
Even a governor said so, ten years later, after first making a joke of it.

6
00:00:21,844 --> 00:00:22,385
Silent.

7
00:00:22,385 --> 00:00:22,771
Slow.

8
00:00:22,771 --> 00:00:23,466
Enormous.

9
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:26,789
But that same night, a second thing happened.

10
00:00:26,789 --> 00:00:30,216
A row of lights, hanging over the city at ten o'clock.

11
00:00:30,216 --> 00:00:33,200
And the story you know blends the two into one.

12
00:00:33,666 --> 00:00:36,165
Tonight we split the case in half.

13
00:00:36,165 --> 00:00:38,444
File A: the V, at eight thirty.

14
00:00:38,444 --> 00:00:40,208
File B: the row, at ten.

15
00:00:40,208 --> 00:00:45,133
Each gets its own evidence, its own explanation, and its own score.

16
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:48,675
Then we ask how two events became one legend.

17
00:00:48,675 --> 00:00:51,000
The clock starts at five to eight.

18
00:00:55,466 --> 00:00:58,229
Seven fifty-five, Henderson, Nevada.

19
00:00:58,229 --> 00:01:02,834
A witness reports a large V-shaped object heading southeast.

20
00:01:02,834 --> 00:01:05,366
It is the first call in the file.

21
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:14,072
Twenty minutes later, near Paulden, Arizona, a former police officer phones the National UFO Reporting Center.

22
00:01:14,072 --> 00:01:16,019
Red-orange lights, in a V.

23
00:01:16,019 --> 00:01:18,566
Then another witness, and another.

24
00:01:19,033 --> 00:01:21,059
Why were so many people outside?

25
00:01:21,059 --> 00:01:26,567
Because Comet Hale-Bopp was at its best that month, and the whole state was looking up.

26
00:01:26,567 --> 00:01:31,000
Skeptic Robert Sheaffer notes it was one of the best nights to see it.

27
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:33,607
So these are not a few cranks.

28
00:01:33,607 --> 00:01:41,598
These are ordinary people, with a clear sky, looking up on purpose, along a line about three hundred miles long.

29
00:01:41,598 --> 00:01:45,166
MUFON later collected over two hundred statements.

30
00:01:45,633 --> 00:01:48,927
Their descriptions disagree in useful ways.

31
00:01:48,927 --> 00:01:51,762
Some saw five lights, some saw seven.

32
00:01:51,762 --> 00:01:54,673
A V, a boomerang, a crown, a triangle.

33
00:01:54,673 --> 00:02:00,266
A few described a dark solid shape, with the stars blocked out behind it.

34
00:02:00,733 --> 00:02:02,207
Notice what that is.

35
00:02:02,207 --> 00:02:06,926
People describing the same event, but disagreeing on what it is.

36
00:02:06,926 --> 00:02:08,400
The lights are data.

37
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,833
The solid body is interpretation.

38
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:12,705
Remember that split.

39
00:02:12,705 --> 00:02:14,392
It is the key to File A.

40
00:02:14,392 --> 00:02:17,133
Now follow the V south, toward Phoenix.

41
00:02:17,599 --> 00:02:18,996
Eight thirty, Phoenix.

42
00:02:18,996 --> 00:02:25,533
Witnesses in the north of the city watch five lights approach from the northwest, and cross the valley.

43
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,786
They describe a silent, slow formation.

44
00:02:28,786 --> 00:02:31,859
Some say they saw stars between the lights.

45
00:02:31,859 --> 00:02:35,432
Others say the stars vanished as the shape passed.

46
00:02:35,432 --> 00:02:37,433
Both accounts are on record.

47
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:42,709
From reports like these came the headline: one craft, a mile wide.

48
00:02:42,709 --> 00:02:52,766
That figure grew in later accounts gathered by researchers such as Doctor Lynne Kitei, some placing a huge object over Sky Harbor Airport.

49
00:02:53,233 --> 00:02:56,801
Glendale, between eight thirty and eight forty-five.

50
00:02:56,801 --> 00:03:02,633
Witnesses see the formation pass overhead, high enough to be swallowed by thin cloud.

51
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:07,156
Something that fades into thin cloud is above that cloud.

52
00:03:07,156 --> 00:03:08,365
High, and silent.

53
00:03:08,365 --> 00:03:13,133
That is exactly how an aircraft at altitude sounds from the ground.

54
00:03:13,599 --> 00:03:18,302
Then the formation crosses the city, heading south toward Tucson.

55
00:03:18,302 --> 00:03:19,605
It does not hover.

56
00:03:19,605 --> 00:03:20,835
It does not dart.

57
00:03:20,835 --> 00:03:25,900
It keeps a steady pace, along the same corridor that air traffic uses.

58
00:03:26,366 --> 00:03:27,747
And there is a video.

59
00:03:27,747 --> 00:03:29,918
The one clear recording of the V.

60
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:33,732
Watch the lights in it, and they shift against each other.

61
00:03:33,732 --> 00:03:35,705
They are not fixed to a frame.

62
00:03:35,705 --> 00:03:38,533
They are separate objects, flying together.

63
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,218
Could one giant craft carry lights that move?

64
00:03:42,218 --> 00:03:43,720
As a hypothesis, yes.

65
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:46,366
But nothing in the video requires it.

66
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:49,586
By nine, the V is gone to the south.

67
00:03:49,586 --> 00:03:54,864
File A now holds two stories: a giant craft, or a flight of aircraft.

68
00:03:54,864 --> 00:03:56,700
Time to test the second.

69
00:03:57,166 --> 00:03:59,658
File A, test one: the telescope.

70
00:03:59,658 --> 00:04:07,599
In Scottsdale, amateur astronomer Mitch Stanley has set up a large Dobsonian telescope, for the comet.

71
00:04:08,066 --> 00:04:09,554
He turns it on the V.

72
00:04:09,554 --> 00:04:13,452
And under magnification, each light splits into a pair.

73
00:04:13,452 --> 00:04:15,933
One on each tip of a squarish wing.

74
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:17,402
Squarish wings.

75
00:04:17,402 --> 00:04:19,140
Not swept, not triangular.

76
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:23,820
He follows the planes for about a minute, then goes back to the comet.

77
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:25,691
His words: they were planes.

78
00:04:25,691 --> 00:04:28,699
There was no way he could have mistaken that.

79
00:04:29,166 --> 00:04:30,786
Test two: the corridor.

80
00:04:30,786 --> 00:04:33,603
Robert Sheaffer reconstructs the flight.

81
00:04:33,603 --> 00:04:41,419
Five A-10 Warthogs from the Operation Snowbird training programme had flown from Tucson to Nellis days earlier.

82
00:04:41,419 --> 00:04:44,800
It was the last night, so they were flying home.

83
00:04:45,266 --> 00:04:53,431
On that reconstruction, they flew by visual rules, in formation, wearing formation lights that look like landing lights.

84
00:04:53,431 --> 00:04:58,466
They crossed Phoenix, and landed at Davis-Monthan around eight forty-five.

85
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:08,023
Analyst Tim Printy modelled the lights at high altitude, around thirty-five to forty thousand feet, where jets cannot be heard.

86
00:05:08,023 --> 00:05:10,600
It is a model, not a measured track.

87
00:05:11,066 --> 00:05:12,554
Here is the weakness.

88
00:05:12,554 --> 00:05:15,529
That flight was never publicly identified.

89
00:05:15,529 --> 00:05:26,933
Luke Air Force Base radar operators saw nothing unusual, and nobody asked the FAA for its radar tapes within two weeks, when such records were routinely deleted.

90
00:05:27,399 --> 00:05:28,881
So File A stays open.

91
00:05:28,881 --> 00:05:35,020
Aircraft in formation is the strongest explanation, with an eyewitness at the eyepiece.

92
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:38,266
But the paperwork that would prove it is gone.

93
00:05:38,733 --> 00:05:39,558
Ten o'clock.

94
00:05:39,558 --> 00:05:41,895
A different sky, different lights.

95
00:05:41,895 --> 00:05:46,637
Over the southwest of Phoenix, a row of bright orange lights appears.

96
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:48,699
About nine of them, in an arc.

97
00:05:49,166 --> 00:05:51,109
They do not move like the V.

98
00:05:51,109 --> 00:05:51,803
They hang.

99
00:05:51,803 --> 00:05:52,982
Some slowly sink.

100
00:05:52,982 --> 00:05:55,064
Thousands of people film them.

101
00:05:55,064 --> 00:05:59,366
This is the footage that was on the news, and on every poster.

102
00:05:59,833 --> 00:06:04,445
Doctor Lynne Kitei, a Phoenix physician, films them from her home.

103
00:06:04,445 --> 00:06:07,030
Others film from all over the valley.

104
00:06:07,030 --> 00:06:11,433
When the tapes air nationally that June, a media frenzy begins.

105
00:06:11,899 --> 00:06:17,647
Sky Harbor air traffic controller Bill Grava sees them on the southern horizon.

106
00:06:17,647 --> 00:06:18,957
His first thought?

107
00:06:18,957 --> 00:06:19,466
Flares.

108
00:06:19,933 --> 00:06:20,947
And notice this.

109
00:06:20,947 --> 00:06:27,600
From every camera, in every part of the valley, the lights sit in the southwest, over the same ridgeline.

110
00:06:28,066 --> 00:06:31,279
A little after ten, they go out one by one.

111
00:06:31,279 --> 00:06:36,733
Not by flying away, but by dropping behind the Sierra Estrella mountains.

112
00:06:37,199 --> 00:06:40,053
A row of lights that sinks behind a ridge.

113
00:06:40,053 --> 00:06:41,276
Hold that thought.

114
00:06:41,276 --> 00:06:44,333
The official answer arrived four months late.

115
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:45,330
File B.

116
00:06:45,330 --> 00:06:50,336
The explanation comes on July twenty-fifth, nineteen ninety-seven.

117
00:06:50,336 --> 00:06:55,266
Captain Drew Sullins, of the Maryland Air National Guard, speaks.

118
00:06:55,733 --> 00:07:01,288
Eight of his unit's A-10s had trained that night over the Barry Goldwater range.

119
00:07:01,288 --> 00:07:05,594
They dropped high-intensity flares from fifteen thousand feet.

120
00:07:05,594 --> 00:07:09,899
The flares fall slowly on parachutes and light up a huge area.

121
00:07:10,366 --> 00:07:16,833
Before flying home, he says, the pilots dumped all their remaining flares at high altitude.

122
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:20,600
One pilot called the result one hell of a light show.

123
00:07:21,066 --> 00:07:31,084
An Arizona National Guard officer, Captain Eileen Bienz, had already put the drop at ten p.m., over the range southwest of Phoenix.

124
00:07:31,084 --> 00:07:31,849
Same hour.

125
00:07:31,849 --> 00:07:34,066
Same direction as the lights.

126
00:07:34,533 --> 00:07:36,360
Then television tested it.

127
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:46,899
Channel Twelve filmed military planes dropping flares, and the result looked, in reporter Tony Ortega's words, remarkably like the ten o'clock lights.

128
00:07:47,366 --> 00:07:48,500
And the hovering?

129
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:55,699
A flare falls slowly under its parachute, and the heat rising from it holds the parachute up like a balloon.

130
00:07:55,699 --> 00:07:57,300
The ridge then hides it.

131
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,633
That is the sinking.

132
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:00,217
Why four months?

133
00:08:00,217 --> 00:08:08,181
Sullins blamed a miscommunication, saying Davis-Monthan checked its resident aircraft logs, not the visiting ones.

134
00:08:08,181 --> 00:08:15,166
Phoenix councilwoman Frances Barwood called the answer too convenient, and asked for a re-enactment.

135
00:08:15,633 --> 00:08:16,700
Doubts remain.

136
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:25,085
Optical physicist Bruce Maccabee triangulated two videos and put the lights some seventy to eighty miles away.

137
00:08:25,085 --> 00:08:28,668
Doctor Kitei says her footage cannot be flares.

138
00:08:28,668 --> 00:08:30,574
Skeptics are unconvinced.

139
00:08:30,574 --> 00:08:34,766
Still, File B is as close to closed as a UFO case gets.

140
00:08:35,233 --> 00:08:37,309
June, nineteen ninety-seven.

141
00:08:37,309 --> 00:08:44,429
The tapes are on national television, and Arizona's governor, Fife Symington, is under pressure.

142
00:08:44,429 --> 00:08:47,766
He is a pilot and a former Air Force officer.

143
00:08:48,233 --> 00:08:51,807
On June nineteenth he announces a state investigation.

144
00:08:51,807 --> 00:08:57,299
Then, the same day, he calls a press conference to say they have found the culprit.

145
00:08:57,766 --> 00:09:02,805
A tall creature in a mask is led in, in handcuffs, before the cameras.

146
00:09:02,805 --> 00:09:04,245
Then it is unmasked.

147
00:09:04,245 --> 00:09:07,700
It is the governor's chief of staff, Jay Heiler.

148
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:08,852
The room laughs.

149
00:09:08,852 --> 00:09:11,299
For a while, the story goes quiet.

150
00:09:11,766 --> 00:09:12,446
Why do it?

151
00:09:12,446 --> 00:09:18,293
Symington later said he wanted to lighten the mood and break the momentum of hysteria.

152
00:09:18,293 --> 00:09:23,733
At the time, he also faced federal fraud charges, and did not need more trouble.

153
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:25,492
The joke had a cost.

154
00:09:25,492 --> 00:09:30,600
For ten years it hung over every witness who said they had seen something real.

155
00:09:31,066 --> 00:09:44,766
Meanwhile, a May nineteen ninety-seven reply from Luke Air Force Base to a Freedom of Information request says it had no records, was not an air-defense base, and had no involvement with the lights.

156
00:09:45,233 --> 00:09:46,822
That fits both stories.

157
00:09:46,822 --> 00:09:52,417
No involvement from Luke fits a flight of Guard jets passing through from Tucson.

158
00:09:52,417 --> 00:09:55,733
And it fits a cover-up, to anyone who wants one.

159
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,322
March, two thousand and seven.

160
00:09:58,322 --> 00:10:01,647
Ten years on, Symington says he saw it himself.

161
00:10:01,647 --> 00:10:06,033
He tells a news network, and later writes it in his own words.

162
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:12,206
A massive delta-shaped craft, he says, gliding silently over a Phoenix mountain.

163
00:10:12,206 --> 00:10:16,700
A solid structure, with enormous lights along its leading edge.

164
00:10:17,166 --> 00:10:20,215
He says he knows every machine that flies.

165
00:10:20,215 --> 00:10:23,845
It did not resemble anything man-made he had seen.

166
00:10:23,845 --> 00:10:29,000
And it was not flares, he says, because flares do not fly in formation.

167
00:10:29,466 --> 00:10:31,186
Take his word seriously.

168
00:10:31,186 --> 00:10:33,479
He was there, and he is a pilot.

169
00:10:33,479 --> 00:10:40,070
But it is retrospective testimony, given a decade later, with no instrument record attached.

170
00:10:40,070 --> 00:10:43,366
And flares explain only one of the two events.

171
00:10:43,833 --> 00:10:45,784
Meanwhile the legend grows.

172
00:10:45,784 --> 00:10:57,133
A fictional thriller, The Phoenix Incident, premiered at a UFO conference in twenty sixteen, mixing real footage with alien monsters and a military cover-up.

173
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:05,748
Skeptic Robert Sheaffer reports that while the audience watched, the Guard was dropping flares over the same range again.

174
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:07,566
Nobody in the room noticed.

175
00:11:08,033 --> 00:11:10,338
So how did two events become one?

176
00:11:10,338 --> 00:11:12,852
The V had no explanation for months.

177
00:11:12,852 --> 00:11:15,716
The row had a good one, but it came late.

178
00:11:15,716 --> 00:11:20,466
Anyone who saw the V and then heard about flares could feel lied to.

179
00:11:20,933 --> 00:11:23,540
That is the real engine of this legend.

180
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:24,610
Not a spaceship.

181
00:11:24,610 --> 00:11:32,700
A gap, between what thousands saw, and what officials took months to say, and never fully documented for the first event.

182
00:11:33,166 --> 00:11:33,667
Debrief.

183
00:11:33,667 --> 00:11:35,733
Time to score the Phoenix Lights.

184
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,974
Two separate events that night: evidence.

185
00:11:38,974 --> 00:11:43,372
The ten o'clock row was flares, confirmed by the Guard: evidence.

186
00:11:43,372 --> 00:11:48,109
The V was separate lights moving together, on the one video: evidence.

187
00:11:48,109 --> 00:11:54,266
A formation of high-altitude aircraft: likely, with a witness at a telescope, but unproven.

188
00:11:54,733 --> 00:11:58,376
The flight's records and radar: never obtained.

189
00:11:58,376 --> 00:12:01,941
One craft a mile wide: no supporting evidence.

190
00:12:01,941 --> 00:12:04,266
Alien spacecraft: no evidence.

191
00:12:04,733 --> 00:12:05,536
The verdict.

192
00:12:05,536 --> 00:12:06,875
Two events, not one.

193
00:12:06,875 --> 00:12:09,218
The ten o'clock lights were flares.

194
00:12:09,218 --> 00:12:15,444
The V was most likely a formation of aircraft, and the paperwork that would prove it is lost.

195
00:12:15,444 --> 00:12:18,054
The Phoenix Lights are not a spaceship.

196
00:12:18,054 --> 00:12:20,933
They are a lesson in how a mystery is made.

197
00:12:21,399 --> 00:12:25,993
On a warm night in March, thousands of people looked up at the same sky.

198
00:12:25,993 --> 00:12:27,907
They really did see something.

199
00:12:27,907 --> 00:12:31,033
They just were not all looking at the same thing.

200
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:38,859
Next case: a pillar of iron, sixteen hundred years old, standing in the open in Delhi, with almost no rust.

201
00:12:38,859 --> 00:12:40,166
A lost super-metal?

202
00:12:40,633 --> 00:12:42,366
What do you think the V was?

203
00:12:42,366 --> 00:12:47,566
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.
